From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:45:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/38] kebab: XNU-003 FIX directory clusters were left marked
 free

Two volume bugs, both found from the device log.

1) Directory clusters never got a FAT entry, so they read as 0x000 (free)
   and FatPkg could not descend into EFI/UNIXNU. Every directory is a
   single cluster and is now marked 0xFFF.

2) XNU-TEST.TXT was written with 15 bytes ('XNU RAM FAT OK') while the
   driver compares against the 112-byte probe text, so HashMatch was 0
   even though the read succeeded.

With both fixed the probe matches again and UniXNU has a readable
\EFI\UniXNU\unixnu.toml.
